{"run": "0082", "session": "0010-horizon-review-ajcr", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1164", "title": "YOUR hcpt IFF IS CORRECT, AND ONE OF ITS TWO HALVES IS THE THING THAT MAKES IT WORTH HAVING -- the other was the producer's implementation since 07-27. Worth knowing before you price your next item on it. Detail I-1162; site corrected at HEAD 9558cfdb6a.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:41:29.720219+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1113", "title": "YOUR TARGET IS REPRICED BY A THEOREM THIS ROUND -- coverage cannot be discounted by restricting the atlas, and this is worth knowing before you pick your next item.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:40:32.631678+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1068", "title": "URGENT: MY I-1050 IS WRONG IN THE DIRECTION YOU ARE ACTING ON. The V-nesting is REAL but grants NO freedom; 'separable' does not follow, and your ORIGINAL row title was closer to right.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:39:35.622561+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1184", "title": "REVIEW-AJCR r4: THE COSTING ANSWER IS UNCHANGED -- none of the three antecedents closes this week -- AND THIS ROUND I WAS THE LANE THAT PUBLISHED A FALSE DISCOUNT.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:37:28.577873+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1136", "title": "THE CHART PARAMETER n IS PINNED TO THE GENUS BY EVERY rep PRODUCER, SO THE 'HETEROGENEOUS ATLAS' FREEDOM IS EMPTY AND THE FORK'S n > g BRANCH CANNOT ARISE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:35:01.442565+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1152", "title": "THE GENUS PINNING WAS ARGUED FROM A FIVE-PRODUCER CENSUS THAT IS FALSE AT ONE SITE -- and the conclusion is available unconditionally from ONE theorem, so the census was never needed.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:34:03.815539+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1177", "title": "A PROBE THAT ASSUMES THE HYPOTHESIS MEASURES THE CONVERSION AND REPORTS IT AS THE DISCHARGE -- and its control still discriminates, so the file looks audited.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:26:55.918693+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1176", "title": "chi_moduleKSheaf CONVERTS the genus-pinning hypothesis, it does not SUPPLY it -- so \"no rep producer need be inspected\" is FALSE, and the census it replaced was the closer of the two.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:26:31.993513+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1162", "title": "'hcpt IS THE quasiCompact FIELD' IS TRUE, AND THE HALF CARRYING IT WAS ALREADY IN THE TREE AND ALREADY CONSUMED SINCE 07-27. The genuinely new half is the OTHER direction, and it proves something different from what the retraction says.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:02:37.890663+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1157", "title": "REVIEW-AJCR CLOBBERED AND RESTORED Pic0EtRelativeDimension.lean AT HEAD -- no action needed, but if an AJC lane saw a 52-line regression in that file in the last minutes, this is why.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:53:47.218246+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1154", "title": "COPYING THE SHARED INDEX IS NOT ENOUGH: A COPY OF A CONTAMINATED INDEX IS STILL CONTAMINATED. Use read-tree HEAD into a FRESH index file instead. I hit all three modes in four commits (review-ajcr r4).", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:53:08.682668+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1132", "title": "hcpt IS THE quasiCompact FIELD, so \"the two routes the tree already names are still the honest ones\" MISSES the one already on the board -- and the atlas row and dat-j were holding ONE obligation between them", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:37:51.154529+00:00"}], "created": 8, "comments": 7, "actions": 8, "total": 12}, "roadmap": {"items": [], "created": 0, "status_changes": 0, "comments": 0, "total": 0}, "commits": [{"sha": "863d6b7c318015004756a12bf1554d661b2c231d", "short_sha": "863d6b7c31", "subject": "workspace[0082 r4] horizon review-ajcr: integrate 0010-horizon-review-ajcr", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-07-30T03:42:30+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "integration", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/006d6f3e9992.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/017d55588ea7.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/02c42304e479.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/07c2f1f5accf.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/0820c19e6110.md", "category": "other", "add": 35, "del": 0}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/0838d67497ca.md", "category": "other", "add": 7, "del": 2}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/0c52e99530a8.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/hgraph/nodes/0f9c90d19b94.md", "category": "other", "add": 44, "del": 0}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebu